{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Commit exactly the named repo-relative paths, whatever happened to them - modified, new, or DELETED. git is the witness (add -A -- <paths> stages a deletion as readily as an edit), so nothing depends on the live store still knowing a record: this is how a removed record, facet, legacy _patches journal, publish metadata (_APPS), generated source, or ordinary file gets committed. Pathspecs are literal (no glob magic) and the commit carries the same pathspec, so pre-staged unrelated work stays staged, untouched. paths is a JSONArray of strings - typically the `path` of every item in one dev.git.store_status group, or of its other_paths; absolute paths and '..' are refused; a path neither tracked nor on disk is skipped and reported. Returns FLAT {status, committed (false = nothing in the paths had changed), paths, skipped, out}.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"paths","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"message","type":"String"},{"name":"author","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"syixmu1a1c65a566fh1","readers":[],"time":1794329496485,"username":"system","writers":[]}